Cell["\<\
A vertex belongs exactly when both endpoint distances equal half the finite \
endpoint distance. Odd distance and disconnected endpoints give an empty \
family; equal anchors give one point. This differs from the segment \
\"Midpoint\" measurement, which retains middle-layer construction density and \
can contain two layers.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e1c7814f-6333-42d6-b46a-9dcaf67fd951"],

Cell["\<\
The graph must be finite, simple, undirected and unweighted, with valid \
anchors. Omitted count or Automatic gives one uniformly random vertex; an \
empty pool gives {}. An integer gives that many distinct vertices, or {} when \
too few exist. UpTo[n] gives at most n distinct vertices; All gives the \
complete pool in graph vertex order. Zero gives {}; negative counts and \
unsupported options stay unevaluated.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9ca21662-0a5c-4263-aa94-4f15860d8c50"],

Cell["\<\
\"NextVertexFunction\" defaults to Automatic. Identity selects in graph \
vertex order. These are the only supported selector values. All and Identity \
do not advance random state. List-valued points remain intact. For an \
empty-List vertex, All and count 1 distinguish {{}} from an empty pool.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0f6028d1-1e14-424f-b896-0077b55682dd"]
}, Open  ]],

